.TH tapectl-db-backup 1  "tapectl-db-backup " 
.SH NAME
tapectl\-db\-backup \- Back up the database, and optionally the private key directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtapectl db backup\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] <\fB\-\-to\fR> [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-include\-keys\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Back up the database, and optionally the private key directory
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-to\fR \fI<TO>\fR
The backup file to write. Its directory must already exist
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without making changes. Commands that cannot preview refuse the flag rather than ignore it
.TP
\fB\-\-include\-keys\fR
Also copy the private key directory, into a directory beside the backup named for it with its extension replaced by `.keys` (`\-\-to /mnt/usb/tapectl.db` copies the keys to `/mnt/usb/tapectl.keys/`). Off by default — the database alone is the common backup case. Private key material copied this way must be treated as secret wherever the destination ends up (USB stick, network share, cloud\-synced folder, ...)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip ADR\-0008 Tier\-2 confirmation prompts. It never reaches a Tier\-3 refusal — those are facts, not risks to accept
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config file.

NOTE: on its own this ALSO relocates the whole tapectl home to the config file\*(Aqs parent directory — database, keys, staging, stage reports. That is how every test harness gets an isolated home, so it still works, but it is surprising enough that it now warns. Use \-\-home when you mean "operate on a different archive", and \-\-config only to point at a config file inside that home.
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
tapectl home directory: database, keys, catalogs, stage\-reports, logs.

Defaults to ~/.tapectl. The config file is taken from <home>/config.toml unless \-\-config overrides it. Also settable as TAPECTL_HOME.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
